{
  "tema": 5230,
  "slug": "comi-preterito-er-ir",
  "titulo": "-er and -ir verbs in the preterite",
  "subtitulo": "Comí tacos y luego salí a caminar.",
  "foto": "t05.jpg",
  "regla": "Regular -er and -ir verbs share the same preterite endings: drop -er/-ir and add -í, -iste, -ió, -imos, -ieron (comí, comiste, comió, comimos, comieron).",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In the preterite, **-er** and **-ir** verbs have **one set of endings**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "com- / viv-",
            "+",
            "-í / -iste / -ió / -imos / -ieron"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "Ending",
            "comer",
            "salir",
            "escribir"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "**-í**",
              "comí",
              "salí",
              "escribí"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "**-iste**",
              "comiste",
              "saliste",
              "escribiste"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "**-ió**",
              "comió",
              "salió",
              "escribió"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "**-imos**",
              "comimos",
              "salimos",
              "escribimos"
            ],
            [
              "ellos, ustedes",
              "**-ieron**",
              "comieron",
              "salieron",
              "escribieron"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Accents only on **yo (-í)** and **él/ella (-ió)**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "For **-er** verbs, **nosotros** changes: **comemos** (now) → **comimos** (past). For **-ir** verbs it's the same: **vivimos** = _we live_ or _we lived_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Stem-changing **-er** verbs lose the change: **volver** → **volví**, **entender** → **entendí**. (-ir verbs like **pedir** and **dormir** keep a change in él and ellos: see Related rules.)"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: think of **-í** as a dot that closes the sentence: comí. Done."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Anoche ==comí== en un puesto de tacos de la Revolución.",
              "en": "Last night I ate at a taco stand on Revolución."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿A qué hora ==saliste== del gimnasio?",
              "en": "What time did you leave the gym?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi primo ==vendió== su carro la semana pasada.",
              "en": "My cousin sold his car last week."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Aprendimos== una barrida nueva en la clase de jiu-jitsu.",
              "en": "We learned a new sweep in jiu-jitsu class."
            },
            {
              "es": "Los tomates ==crecieron== mucho este verano.",
              "en": "The tomatoes grew a lot this summer."
            },
            {
              "es": "Le ==escribí== un correo al casero.",
              "en": "I wrote an email to the landlord."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Ustedes ==vivieron== en Ensenada?",
              "en": "Did you guys live in Ensenada?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Ayer ==volví== tarde a la casa.",
              "en": "Yesterday I got home late."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
